	<body>
		<div class="column">
			<a href="../../#extended-library">← back</a>

			<h1 id="polca-dours">Toc d'Entrada a Plaça</h1>
			<p>
				This tune, as the name suggests, is played when the castellers are
				entering the town/city square (plaza) to perform, usually as a parade
				with the musicians in front and the castellers behind. To me is sounds
				lke a fanfare, marking the beginning of a performance.
			</p>

			<YouTube id="PQDA5QbEUkk" title="Música i castells: Entrada a plaça" />
			<YouTube id="Dk3M54iBEno" title="Entrada a Plaça" />
			<YouTube
				id="6zp5gXVLJOE"
				title="Toc d'entrada a la plaça - primera veu"
			/>

			<img
				src="/castells-music/sheet music/Toc d'Entrada a Placa/Toc d'Entrada a placa [solfege].svg"
				alt="Sheet music for Toc d'entrada a Plaça"
			/>

			<p>
				First voice:
				<a
					href="/castells-music/sheet music/Toc d'Entrada a Placa/Toc d'Entrada a placa [solfege].pdf"
